       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant 2,550 mg per day in total. If so, that would be **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals**.\n\nPlease confirm how you'd like to proceed:\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day total), or\n2. A different dose you specify. If you do want 2550 mg per administration, tell me and I'll note that it's intentional.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
